# Folders kept in sync between machines by Syncthing, one per line, relative to ~.
# The folder ID is the name, so it must be the same on every machine.
# Read by install.sh (creates them) and syncthing/pair.sh (shares them).
#
# ~ means your whole home, as one folder with ID "home". What it leaves out is in
# syncthing/stignore (linked to ~/.stignore). With ~ listed, nothing else may be:
# folders must not nest (the outer one would rescan everything the inner one writes).
~
